 @Top-TierSports  about $800 - 820 should be possible with all new parts i just checked. I even included 32gb of ram and not just some cheap budget stuff. If you want to go full budget build under $800 is possible even with new parts. Some people only have a monitor so that logic with the tv can also go the other way around or you can just use your tv and use steamos or bazzite for a more console-like experience if you prefer not to be on a desk with a monitor.

You don't have to upgrade way more on a PC. If i build a PS5 like PC build when the PS5 came out i can stay with that built and retain a similar experience until the end of the PS5 lifecycle.. That PC won't get magically worse just because new parts release and it will stay at that performance level.

Your arguments are superfricial perspectives of what a PC Gamer "should" be and while it's true that the more dedicated PC Gamers often upgrade a lot that still doesn't make it a requirement for the average gamer. The most used GPUs on the Steam Survey (RTX 3060) is now over 4 years old so that's already half of the lifecycle of a console and that's the lowest end model of that generation and people can still play just fine and they will continue to do fine for the next few years just like the PS5.

